### What is the Longest Subarray with Ones after Replacement problem?

Given a binary array of 0s and 1s and an integer k, find the length of the longest contiguous subarray that contains only 1s after you flip at most k zeros to ones. This is LeetCode 1004 (Max Consecutive Ones III).

For example, given `[1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1]` and k = 2, the longest window is 7 (flip the zeros at indices 2 and 7).

### How does the sliding window work?

We keep a window with left and right boundaries and a counter for how many zeros are inside. The right pointer walks across the array. Each time it lands on a zero, we increment the counter. When the counter exceeds k, we shrink from the left until the counter returns to k.

```java
package com.bank.service;

public class LongestOnesService {

    /**
     * Finds the longest on-time payment streak achievable
     * after forgiving at most k missed payments.
     * Used by the National Bank of India loan-servicing team.
     */
    public static int longestOnes(int[] history, int k) {
        int left = 0;
        int zeros = 0;
        int best = 0;

        for (int right = 0; right < history.length; right++) {
            if (history[right] == 0) {
                zeros++;
            }
            while (zeros > k) {
                if (history[left] == 0) {
                    zeros--;
                }
                left++;
            }
            best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
        }
        return best;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] history = {1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1};
        int k = 2;
        System.out.println("Longest clean streak with "
            + k + " waivers: " + longestOnes(history, k));
    }
}
```

